,title,link,text,language,family
0,Oro Win language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oro_Win_language,"November 24, 2025 - Oro Win is a moribund Chapacuran language spoken along the upper stretches of the Pacaás Novos River in Brazil. As of 2010, there were only six known speakers of Oro Win in Brazil, and all of them were over 50 years of age.",Oro Win,Chapacuran
1,Chapacuran languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chapacuran_languages,"2 weeks ago - The Chapacuran languages are a nearly extinct Native American language family of South America. Almost all Chapacuran languages are extinct, and the four that are extant are moribund, with the exception of Wariʼ.",Oro Win,Chapacuran
